[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583648777","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101403#issuecomment-2583648777","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101403","id":2583648777,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Z_1oJ","user":{"login":"twrightsman","id":6300973,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMDA5NzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6300973?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman","html_url":"https://github.com/twrightsman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-10T19:08:36Z","updated_at":"2025-01-10T19:08:36Z","body":"To clarify things a little bit (since I saw @AThousandShips react confused :slightly_smiling_face:), here is an excerpt from the Makefile that Debian uses to install the built binaries:\r\n\r\n```\r\ninstall -D -m 400 $(CURDIR)/bin/godot.editor $(CURDIR)/debian/godot4/usr/bin/godot4\r\ninstall -D -m 400 $(CURDIR)/bin/godot.template-debug $(CURDIR)/debian/godot4-template-debug/usr/bin/godot4-template-debug\r\ninstall -D -m 400 $(CURDIR)/bin/godot.template-release $(CURDIR)/debian/godot4-template-release/usr/bin/godot4-template-release\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith this patch I can just use `bin/godot.editor` (built with `extra_suffix=editor`) instead of trying to match Debian's architecture naming to Godot's architecture naming, which is tedious in a Makefile and doesn't always perfectly map 1-to-1.\r\n\r\nI am of course open to alternative solutions in case I am missing something in Godot's build system.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583648777/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2584934192","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101403#issuecomment-2584934192","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101403","id":2584934192,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aEvcw","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-11T00:01:10Z","updated_at":"2025-01-11T00:01:10Z","body":"@twrightsman hi, thanks for explaining your use case further! IMO your reasoning makes sense.\r\n\r\nI guess you could _technically_ do something like adding a custom suffix with `extra_suffix` and doing something like:\r\n\r\n```\r\nscons extra_suffix=debian #...\r\ninstall -D -m 400 $(CURDIR)/bin/godot.*.editor.*.debian $(CURDIR)/debian/godot4/usr/bin/godot4\r\ninstall -D -m 400 $(CURDIR)/bin/godot.*.template-debug.*.debian $(CURDIR)/debian/godot4-template-debug/usr/bin/godot4-template-debug\r\ninstall -D -m 400 $(CURDIR)/bin/godot.*.template-release.*.debian $(CURDIR)/debian/godot4-template-release/usr/bin/godot4-template-release\r\n```\r\n\r\nOr perhaps, if the debian package format allows, manually specify the SCons `arch` variable while building and use some switch case for mapping them (I think make supports them?). The names should be stable according to _that_. There's a map over at `platform_methods.py`:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/abf8e1e6f9e165ea209350ab9a98f01feca93b90/platform_methods.py#L18-L35\r\n\r\nThe value to each key is, AFAIU, the final string that is attached to the executable.\r\n\r\nBut those approaches are indeed kinda hacky, as they require some luck or constant chasing of project changes, so I agree with your proposal.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2584934192/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2584942306","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101403#issuecomment-2584942306","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101403","id":2584942306,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aExbi","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-11T00:12:31Z","updated_at":"2025-01-11T00:12:46Z","body":"Shouldn't we add a SCons option to customize the output binary name and path instead? For example, `output_path=\"bin/something\"`.\r\n\r\nThis way, you can directly write the binary to the correct path if you wish (then `chmod` it afterwards if needed).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2584942306/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2584954174","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101403#issuecomment-2584954174","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101403","id":2584954174,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aE0U-","user":{"login":"twrightsman","id":6300973,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMDA5NzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6300973?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman","html_url":"https://github.com/twrightsman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-11T00:28:58Z","updated_at":"2025-01-11T00:28:58Z","body":"> Shouldn't we add a SCons option to customize the output binary name and path instead?\r\n\r\nI think this is a perfectly fine solution as well. I started with this one because it was easier to figure out versus trying to follow exactly where SCons determines the final binary name. I'm not yet familiar enough with SCons + Godot's build scripts.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2584954174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3109848425","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101403#issuecomment-3109848425","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101403","id":3109848425,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65XIVp","user":{"login":"twrightsman","id":6300973,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMDA5NzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6300973?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman","html_url":"https://github.com/twrightsman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twrightsman/gists{/gist_i